<Group labelreference="L3" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Font bold="true">MATH 4503/6503 worksheet 2: an introduction to Maple</Font></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Font bold="false">Irfan Javed
<Font italic="true">January 12, 2026</Font></Font></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"><Font opaque="false" subscript="false" underline="false" superscript="false" bold="false" foreground="[0,0,0]" italic="false" executable="false" selection-placeholder="false" size="12" readonly="false" background="[255,255,255]" style="LaTeX" strikethrough="false" placeholder="false" family="Times New Roman" font_style_name="LaTeX">This worksheet is meant to serve as a brief introduction to Maple. It</Font><Font bold="false"> is a powerful piece of softawre that has many applications outside the scope of this course. Here is a nonexclusive list of what it is extremely useful for.</Font></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal" bullet="dot"><Font bold="false">Originally, the package was developed with the purpose of performing (tedious) algebraic manipulation of complicated mathematical expressions. Therefore, it can save one pages and pages of writing when trying to make sense of hideous equations and finding their solutions. Importantly, it does not make mistakes with minus signs, or factors of </Font><Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbW5HRiQ2JVEiMkYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ25vcm1hbEYnRi9GMg==">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbW5HRiQ2JVEiMkYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ25vcm1hbEYnRi9GMg==</Equation><Font bold="false">.</Font></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal" bullet="dot"><Font bold="false">One can use the software to plot functions in two or three dimensions, construct movies, or plot datapoints.</Font></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal" bullet="dot"><Font bold="false">Maple knows calculus. This means it can analytically differentiate anything, integrate lots of things, and solve some differential equations.</Font></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal" bullet="dot"><Font bold="false">However, many of the integrals, differential equations, and ordinary equations one meets during research will be too hard for Maple to solve in closed form. However, all is not lost since the package includes many facilities for constructing numeric solutions to problems.</Font></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal" bullet="dot"><Font bold="false">Lastly, but not least, Maple can act as a fully functional programming language like C++, Python, etc.</Font></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"><Font bold="false">I will attempt to give a brief introduction to some of these topics, but the best way to learn is to play with the software yourself and use the help pages.</Font></Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 1" layout="Heading 1">Fundamentals</Text-field></Title>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 2" layout="Heading 2">Basic syntax</Text-field></Title><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Maple worksheets are broken up into individual components called execution groups. Here is an example of an execution group.</Text-field>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L10" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">sin(0.1);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbW5HNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JFEuMC4wOTk4MzM0MTY2NUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdub3JtYWxGJw==">JCIrbDtNJCkqKiEjNg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L12" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"><Font opaque="false" subscript="false" underline="false" superscript="false" bold="false" foreground="[0,0,0]" italic="false" executable="false" selection-placeholder="false" size="12" readonly="false" background="[255,255,255]" style="LaTeX" strikethrough="false" placeholder="false" family="Times New Roman" font_style_name="LaTeX">The user input in this case is what appears in front of the </Font><Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">&gt;</Font><Font opaque="false" subscript="false" underline="false" superscript="false" bold="false" foreground="[0,0,0]" italic="false" executable="false" selection-placeholder="false" size="12" readonly="false" background="[255,255,255]" style="LaTeX" strikethrough="false" placeholder="false" family="Times New Roman" font_style_name="LaTeX"> sign while the output is the centred text. Notice that the user input here is terminated by a semicolon, &quot;</Font><Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">;</Font><Font opaque="false" subscript="false" underline="false" superscript="false" bold="false" foreground="[0,0,0]" italic="false" executable="false" selection-placeholder="false" size="12" readonly="false" background="[255,255,255]" style="LaTeX" strikethrough="false" placeholder="false" family="Times New Roman" font_style_name="LaTeX">&quot;. Whenever you want Maple to execute a command and print an answer, you must type in the command, end the line with a semicolon, and press ENTER. In this case, I have asked Maple to calculate </Font><Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">sin(0.1)</Font><Font opaque="false" subscript="false" underline="false" superscript="false" bold="false" foreground="[0,0,0]" italic="false" executable="false" selection-placeholder="false" size="12" readonly="false" background="[255,255,255]" style="LaTeX" strikethrough="false" placeholder="false" family="Times New Roman" font_style_name="LaTeX">, and print out the answer. It is possible to have Maple execute a command and not display the answer by terminating the line with a colon, &quot;</Font><Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">:</Font><Font opaque="false" subscript="false" underline="false" superscript="false" bold="false" foreground="[0,0,0]" italic="false" executable="false" selection-placeholder="false" size="12" readonly="false" background="[255,255,255]" style="LaTeX" strikethrough="false" placeholder="false" family="Times New Roman" font_style_name="LaTeX">&quot;, instead. For example, by typing in</Font></Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L13" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">sin(0.1):</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L15" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">and pressing return, I get Maple to calculate <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">sin(0.1)</Font>, but it does not display the result. One can have multiple commands in an execution group. For example,</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L14" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">sin(0.1); cos(0.4); ln(0.2);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbW5HNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JFEuMC4wOTk4MzM0MTY2NUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdub3JtYWxGJw==">JCIrbDtNJCkqKiEjNg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbW5HNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JFEtMC45MjEwNjA5OTQwRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ25vcm1hbEYn">JCIrUyo0MUAqISM1</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbW5HNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JFE1JnVtaW51czA7MS42MDk0Mzc5MTJGJy8lLG1hdGh2YXJpYW50R1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">JCErN3pWNDshIio=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L17" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">You can see that the output of each command is put on a separate line. For clarity, we may want to have each command in an execution group on its own line, which is accomplished by pressing SHIFT+ENTER after the colons or semicolons. This looks like</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L16" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">sin(0.1);
cos(0.4);ln(0.2);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbW5HNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JFEuMC4wOTk4MzM0MTY2NUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdub3JtYWxGJw==">JCIrbDtNJCkqKiEjNg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbW5HNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JFEtMC45MjEwNjA5OTQwRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ25vcm1hbEYn">JCIrUyo0MUAqISM1</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbW5HNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JFE1JnVtaW51czA7MS42MDk0Mzc5MTJGJy8lLG1hdGh2YXJpYW50R1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">JCErN3pWNDshIio=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
</Section>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 2" layout="Heading 2">Defining quantities</Text-field></Title>
<Group labelreference="L22" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">To define a quantity, you use the symbol &quot;<Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">:=</Font>&quot;. That is, a colon followed by an equals sign. For example,</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L20" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">a := sin(x^2);
b := cos(x^2);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSJhR0YoLUkkc2luR0YlNiMqJEkieEdGKCIiIzcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSJiR0YoLUkkY29zR0YlNiMqJEkieEdGKCIiIzcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L23" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Now, whenever <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">a</Font> appears again in the worksheet, Maple will automatically substitute in its definition.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L24" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">c := a^2 + b^2;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSJjR0YoLCYqJC1JJHNpbkdGJTYjKiRJInhHRigiIiNGNSIiIiokLUkkY29zR0YlRjJGNUY2NyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L25" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"><Font opaque="false" subscript="false" underline="false" superscript="false" bold="false" foreground="[0,0,0]" italic="false" executable="false" selection-placeholder="false" size="12" readonly="false" background="[255,255,255]" style="LaTeX" strikethrough="false" placeholder="false" family="Times New Roman" font_style_name="LaTeX">Notice here that </Font><Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">c</Font><Font opaque="false" subscript="false" underline="false" superscript="false" bold="false" foreground="[0,0,0]" italic="false" executable="false" selection-placeholder="false" size="12" readonly="false" background="[255,255,255]" style="LaTeX" strikethrough="false" placeholder="false" family="Times New Roman" font_style_name="LaTeX"> has been </Font>recursively<Font opaque="false" subscript="false" underline="false" superscript="false" bold="false" foreground="[0,0,0]" italic="false" executable="false" selection-placeholder="false" size="12" readonly="false" background="[255,255,255]" style="LaTeX" strikethrough="false" placeholder="false" family="Times New Roman" font_style_name="LaTeX"> defined in terms of </Font><Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">a</Font><Font opaque="false" subscript="false" underline="false" superscript="false" bold="false" foreground="[0,0,0]" italic="false" executable="false" selection-placeholder="false" size="12" readonly="false" background="[255,255,255]" style="LaTeX" strikethrough="false" placeholder="false" family="Times New Roman" font_style_name="LaTeX"> and </Font><Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">b</Font><Font opaque="false" subscript="false" underline="false" superscript="false" bold="false" foreground="[0,0,0]" italic="false" executable="false" selection-placeholder="false" size="12" readonly="false" background="[255,255,255]" style="LaTeX" strikethrough="false" placeholder="false" family="Times New Roman" font_style_name="LaTeX">. As in most programming languages, you can redefine a quantity in terms of its current value:</Font></Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L26" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">c := sqrt(c);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSJjR0YoKiQsJiokLUkkc2luR0YlNiMqJEkieEdGKCIiI0Y2IiIiKiQtSSRjb3NHRiVGM0Y2RjcjRjdGNjcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L28" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Sometimes you want Maple to forget something you have previously defined. To undefine <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">a</Font>, we enter in the following:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L29" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">a := 'a';</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSJhR0YoRi03I0Yt</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L31" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Now, whenever <Font mathvariant="bold" mathbackground="[255,255,255]" fontweight="bold" mathsize="12" fontfamily="Courier New" style="Maple Input" mathcolor="[120,0,14]" executable="false">a</Font> appears, Maple will treat it as an unknown quantity. Finally, you can define a bunch of stuff at once using commas:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L32" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">theta, Theta, q := x, y, z;
theta^2+Theta^2+q^2;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+NiVJJnRoZXRhR0YoSSZUaGV0YUdGKEkicUdGKDYlSSJ4R0YoSSJ5R0YoSSJ6R0YoNyVGMkYzRjQ=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LCgqJEkieEc2IiIiIyIiIiokSSJ5R0YlRiZGJyokSSJ6R0YlRiZGJw==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
</Section>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 2" layout="Heading 2">Multi-element objects: tables, sets, lists, etc.</Text-field></Title>
<Group labelreference="L33" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">restart;</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L34" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Several types of Maple objects can consist of collection of individual elements. The most rudimentary of these is a table, which we can create as follows:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L35" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">a[1] := 1;
a[2] := 4;
a[3] := 0;
print(a);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+JkkiYUdGKDYjIiIiRjA3I0Yw</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+JkkiYUdGKDYjIiIjIiIlNyNGMQ==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+JkkiYUdGKDYjIiIkIiIhNyNGMQ==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyNLSSZUQUJMRUdGJjYjNyUvIiIiRjEvIiIjIiIlLyIiJCIiIVEocHByaW50MEYoNyNJImFHRig=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L36" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">The general rule is that components of multi-element objects are labeled by quantities in square brackets. Note that &quot;indices&quot; are not necessarily numeric:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L37" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">a := 'a':
a[t] := r^2;
a[r] := sin(omega*t);
a[theta] := exp(t-r);
a[phi] := L/r^2;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+JkkiYUdGKDYjSSJ0R0YoKiRJInJHRigiIiM3I0Yx</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+JkkiYUdGKDYjSSJyR0YoLUkkc2luR0YlNiMqJkkmb21lZ2FHRigiIiJJInRHRihGNjcjRjE=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+JkkiYUdGKDYjSSZ0aGV0YUdGKC1JJGV4cEdGJTYjLCZJInRHRigiIiJJInJHRighIiI3I0Yx</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+JkkiYUdGKDYjSSRwaGlHRigqJkkiTEdGKCIiIkkickdGKCEiIzcjRjE=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L38" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Further types of data structures are sets and lists. Both of these are one-dimensional collections of objects, and their chief difference is whether or not ordering is important. A list is a comma-delimited sequence of objects enclosed in square brackets:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L39" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">a := 'a':
a := [1, sin(x^2), int(f(q), q = -infinity..infinity), 1];
a[3];</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L40" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"><Font opaque="false" subscript="false" underline="false" superscript="false" bold="false" foreground="[0,0,0]" italic="false" executable="false" selection-placeholder="false" size="12" readonly="false" background="[255,255,255]" style="LaTeX" strikethrough="false" placeholder="false" family="Times New Roman" font_style_name="LaTeX">On the other hand, a set is a sequence of </Font>distinct<Font opaque="false" subscript="false" underline="false" superscript="false" bold="false" foreground="[0,0,0]" italic="false" executable="false" selection-placeholder="false" size="12" readonly="false" background="[255,255,255]" style="LaTeX" strikethrough="false" placeholder="false" family="Times New Roman" font_style_name="LaTeX"> elements where order is not important. It is defined like a list but with curly brackets:</Font></Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L41" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">a := 'a':
a := {1 = x+(y+z)^3, 0 = sin(x*z/y), 3, 2, 1, 3};</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSJhR0YoPCciIiIiIiMiIiQvIiIhLUkkc2luR0YlNiMqKEkieEdGKEYvSSJ6R0YoRi9JInlHRighIiIvRi8sJkY4Ri8qJCwmRjpGL0Y5Ri9GMUYvNyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L42" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Notice that Maple did not preserve the ordering of elements given in the input, and that the duplicate entry <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">3</Font> was deleted. Finally, you can define <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy8lK2V4ZWN1dGFibGVHUSZmYWxzZUYnL0YzUSdub3JtYWxGJw==">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy8lK2V4ZWN1dGFibGVHUSZmYWxzZUYnL0YzUSdub3JtYWxGJw==</Equation>-dimensional objects known as arrays.  For example, here is a <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbW5HRiQ2JFEiM0YnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdub3JtYWxGJy8lK2V4ZWN1dGFibGVHUSZmYWxzZUYnRi8=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbW5HRiQ2JFEiM0YnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdub3JtYWxGJy8lK2V4ZWN1dGFibGVHUSZmYWxzZUYnRi8=</Equation>-dimensional object:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L43" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">a := Array(1..3, -5..5, 0..2000);
a[1, -5, 1999] := Pi;
a[0, 0, 0] := 5;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+JkkiYUdGKDYlIiIiISImIiUqKj5JI1BpR0YmNyNGMw==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="HyperlinkError" layout="HyperlinkError"><Hyperlink linktarget="http://www.maplesoft.com/support/help/errors/view.aspx?path=Error,%20Array%20index%20out%20of%20range" hyperlink="true"><Font style="HyperlinkError">Error, Array index out of range</Font></Hyperlink></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
</Section>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 2" layout="Heading 2">Useful things to know</Text-field></Title>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 3" layout="Heading 3">Special symbols</Text-field></Title>
<Group labelreference="L68" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Certain symbols have reserved meanings. 3.14... is known as <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">Pi</Font> while Euler's constant is <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">gamma</Font>. To evaluate expressions involving these to floating point accuracy, use <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">evalf</Font>:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L61" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">a := [Pi/2, gamma];
evalf(a);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSJhR0YoNyQsJEkjUGlHRiYjIiIiIiIjSSZnYW1tYUdGJjcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">NyQkIitGanpxOiEiKiQiK1xtOnNkISM1</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L60" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">We have already seen above how <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">infinity</Font> refers to mathematical infinity. A capital <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">I</Font> refers to the square root of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>, i.e., <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L62" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">[I, I^2, I^3];</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">NyVeIyIiIiEiIl4jRiU=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L64" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">You cannot assign values to any of these symbols:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L63" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">I := 2;
Pi := 4;
gamma := 7;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="HyperlinkError" layout="HyperlinkError"><Hyperlink linktarget="http://www.maplesoft.com/support/help/errors/view.aspx?path=Error,%20illegal%20use%20of%20an%20object%20as%20a%20name" hyperlink="true"><Font style="HyperlinkError">Error, illegal use of an object as a name</Font></Hyperlink></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="HyperlinkError" layout="HyperlinkError"><Hyperlink linktarget="http://www.maplesoft.com/support/help/errors/view.aspx?path=Error,%20attempting%20to%20assign%20to%20%60Pi%60%20which%20is%20protected.%20%20Try%20declaring%20%60local%20Pi%60%3B%20see%20%3Fprotect%20for%20details." hyperlink="true"><Font style="HyperlinkError">Error, attempting to assign to `Pi` which is protected.  Try declaring `local Pi`; see ?protect for details.</Font></Hyperlink></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="HyperlinkError" layout="HyperlinkError"><Hyperlink linktarget="http://www.maplesoft.com/support/help/errors/view.aspx?path=Error,%20attempting%20to%20assign%20to%20%60gamma%60%20which%20is%20protected.%20%20Try%20declaring%20%60local%20gamma%60%3B%20see%20%3Fprotect%20for%20details." hyperlink="true"><Font style="HyperlinkError">Error, attempting to assign to `gamma` which is protected.  Try declaring `local gamma`; see ?protect for details.</Font></Hyperlink></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L66" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">One thing that is not a special symbol is <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">e</Font>; that is, <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">e</Font> does not represent the base of the natural logarithm. Rather, <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">e</Font> is just an ordinary variable:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L65" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">e := 2;
e^7;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSJlR0YoIiIjNyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbW5HNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JFEkMTI4RicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ25vcm1hbEYn">IiRHIg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L67" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">If you actually want the base of the natural logarithm, use the function <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">exp</Font>:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L69" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">exp(1);
evalf(exp(1));</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LUkkZXhwRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiNiMiIiI=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbW5HNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JFEsMi43MTgyODE4MjhGJy8lLG1hdGh2YXJpYW50R1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">JCIrRz1HPUYhIio=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
</Section>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 3" layout="Heading 3">Some &quot;essential&quot; commands</Text-field></Title>
<Group labelreference="L73" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Bullet Item" layout="Bullet Item">Issuing a <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">restart</Font> command undefines all variables, something which makes it a useful command to have at the top of a worksheet.</Text-field><Text-field style="Bullet Item" layout="Bullet Item">Under the Exexute menu, there is an &quot;Execute Worksheet'' item, which is self-explanatory.</Text-field><Text-field style="Bullet Item" layout="Bullet Item">The echo character is <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">%</Font>, which inserts the last line of output into the current line of input. To wit,</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L74" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">tanh(1/2);
evalf(%);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LUkldGFuaEc2JCUqcHJvdGVjdGVkR0koX3N5c2xpYkc2IjYjIyIiIiIiIw==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbW5HNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JFEtMC40NjIxMTcxNTczRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ25vcm1hbEYn">JCIrdDo8QFkhIzU=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L76" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Bullet Item" layout="Bullet Item">The comment character is <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">#</Font>. When it appears on a line, the complier ignores everything after it.</Text-field><Text-field style="Bullet Item" layout="Bullet Item">On Windows and Linux, CTRL+J (CTRL+K) inserts a new execution group after (before) the position of the cursor.</Text-field><Text-field style="Bullet Item" layout="Bullet Item">On Macs, CMD+J (CMD+K) inserts a new execution group after (before) the position of the cursor.</Text-field><Text-field style="Bullet Item" layout="Bullet Item">Perhaps most importantly, a question mark followed by a topic opens a help page (no colon/semi-colon needed). Try <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">?evalf</Font><Font mathvariant="normal" mathbackground="[255,255,255]" mathsize="12" fontfamily="Times New Roman" style="Text" mathcolor="[0,0,0]">.</Font></Text-field><Text-field style="Bullet Item" layout="Bullet Item">By default, Maple calcuates floating point numbers to <Equation executable="false" style="Bullet Item" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbW5HRiQ2JFEjMTBGJy8lLG1hdGh2YXJpYW50R1Enbm9ybWFsRidGLw==">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbW5HRiQ2JFEjMTBGJy8lLG1hdGh2YXJpYW50R1Enbm9ybWFsRidGLw==</Equation> digit accuracy. If you want more, redefine <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">Digits</Font>:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L77" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">evalf(exp(1));
Digits := 30;
evalf(exp(1));
Digits := 10;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbW5HNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JFEsMi43MTgyODE4MjhGJy8lLG1hdGh2YXJpYW50R1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">JCIrRz1HPUYhIio=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSdEaWdpdHNHRigiI0k3I0Yu</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbW5HNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JFFAMi43MTgyODE4Mjg0NTkwNDUyMzUzNjAyODc0NzEzNUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdub3JtYWxGJw==">JCI/TnJ1R2dgQlghZiVHPUc9RiEjSA==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSdEaWdpdHNHRigiIzU3I0Yu</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L79" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Rule of thumb for Digits is as follows: you can set it up to <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbW5HRiQ2JFEjMTRGJy8lLG1hdGh2YXJpYW50R1Enbm9ybWFsRicvJStleGVjdXRhYmxlR1EmZmFsc2VGJ0Yv">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbW5HRiQ2JFEjMTRGJy8lLG1hdGh2YXJpYW50R1Enbm9ybWFsRicvJStleGVjdXRhYmxlR1EmZmFsc2VGJ0Yv</Equation> without sacrificing speed or memory, but more than this will increase the CPU time for numeric calculations.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
</Section>
</Section>
</Section>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 1" layout="Heading 1">Manipulating expressions</Text-field></Title>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 2" layout="Heading 2">Simplification</Text-field></Title>
<Group labelreference="L413" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">restart;</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L412" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">First and foremost, Maple is a symbolic computation language, so what it was created to do is algebraically simplify complex expressions by applying various algorithms. The easiest way to access this functionality is to use the <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">simplify</Font> command.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L415" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">expr := sin(x)^2+cos(x)^2;
simplify(expr);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSVleHByR0YoLCYqJC1JJHNpbkdGJTYjSSJ4R0YoIiIjIiIiKiQtSSRjb3NHRiVGMkY0RjU3I0Yu</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbW5HNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JFEiMUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdub3JtYWxGJw==">IiIi</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L414" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">In and of itself, <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">simplify</Font> is a bit of a brute force command that might not give you what you want. The alternatives <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">expand</Font> and <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">factor</Font> perform more specific tasks:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L417" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">expr_1 := (a+c*b)^3*(a-c);
simplify(expr_1);
expr_2 := expand(expr_1);
factor(expr_2);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSdleHByXzFHRigqJiwmKiZJImJHRigiIiJJImNHRihGMkYySSJhR0YoRjIiIiQsJkY0RjJGMyEiIkYyNyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">KiYsJiomSSJiRzYiIiIiSSJjR0YmRidGJ0kiYUdGJkYnIiIkLCZGKUYnRighIiJGJw==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSdleHByXzJHRigsMiooSSJhR0YoIiIiSSJiR0YoIiIkSSJjR0YoRjNGMSomRjJGM0Y0IiIlISIiKihGMCIiI0YyRjlGNEY5RjMqKEYwRjFGMkY5RjRGMyEiJCooRjBGM0YyRjFGNEYxRjMqKEYwRjlGMkYxRjRGOUY7KiRGMEY2RjEqJkYwRjNGNEYxRjc3I0Yu</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">KiYsJiomSSJiRzYiIiIiSSJjR0YmRidGJ0kiYUdGJkYnIiIkLCZGKUYnRighIiJGJw==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L416" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">The <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">collect</Font> and <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">coeff</Font> commands are convenient for the manipulation of polynomials like <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">expr_2</Font> above:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L423" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">collect(expr_2, a);
expr_3 := collect(expr_2, a, factor);
coeff(expr_3, a^2);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LCwqJEkiYUc2IiIiJSIiIiomLCYqJkkiYkdGJUYnSSJjR0YlRiciIiRGLCEiIkYnRiRGLUYnKiYsJiomRisiIiNGLEYyRi0qJkYrRidGLEYyISIkRidGJEYyRicqJiwmKiZGK0YtRixGLUYnKiZGK0YyRixGLUY0RidGJEYnRicqJkYrRi1GLEYmRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSdleHByXzNHRigsLCokSSJhR0YoIiIlIiIiKihJImNHRihGMiwmSSJiR0YoIiIkISIiRjJGMkYwRjdGMioqRjQiIiNGNkYyLCZGNkYyRjhGMkYyRjBGOkY3KipGNkY6RjRGNywmRjZGMiEiJEYyRjJGMEYyRjIqJkY2RjdGNEYxRjg3I0Yu</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LCQqKEkiY0c2IiIiI0kiYkdGJSIiIiwmRidGKCEiIkYoRigiIiQ=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L427" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal"><Font opaque="false" subscript="false" underline="false" superscript="false" bold="false" foreground="[0,0,0]" italic="false" executable="false" selection-placeholder="false" size="12" readonly="false" background="[255,255,255]" style="LaTeX" strikethrough="false" placeholder="false" family="Times New Roman" font_style_name="LaTeX">The second command reads the following in words: &quot;rewrite </Font><Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">expr_2</Font><Font opaque="false" subscript="false" underline="false" superscript="false" bold="false" foreground="[0,0,0]" italic="false" executable="false" selection-placeholder="false" size="12" readonly="false" background="[255,255,255]" style="LaTeX" strikethrough="false" placeholder="false" family="Times New Roman" font_style_name="LaTeX"> such that each term contains a single power of </Font><Equation executable="false" style="Normal" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiYUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiYUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation><Font opaque="false" subscript="false" underline="false" superscript="false" bold="false" foreground="[0,0,0]" italic="false" executable="false" selection-placeholder="false" size="12" readonly="false" background="[255,255,255]" style="LaTeX" strikethrough="false" placeholder="false" family="Times New Roman" font_style_name="LaTeX">, and then factor each coefficient in the sum.'' The third command answers the question &quot;what is the coefficient of </Font><Equation executable="false" style="Normal" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUklbXN1cEdGJDYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiYUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy1GIzYlLUkjbW5HRiQ2JFEiMkYnL0Y2USdub3JtYWxGJ0YyRjUvJTFzdXBlcnNjcmlwdHNoaWZ0R1EiMEYnRj4=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUklbXN1cEdGJDYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiYUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy1GIzYlLUkjbW5HRiQ2JFEiMkYnL0Y2USdub3JtYWxGJ0YyRjUvJTFzdXBlcnNjcmlwdHNoaWZ0R1EiMEYnRj4=</Equation><Font opaque="false" subscript="false" underline="false" superscript="false" bold="false" foreground="[0,0,0]" italic="false" executable="false" selection-placeholder="false" size="12" readonly="false" background="[255,255,255]" style="LaTeX" strikethrough="false" placeholder="false" family="Times New Roman" font_style_name="LaTeX"> in </Font><Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">expr_3</Font><Font opaque="false" subscript="false" underline="false" superscript="false" bold="false" foreground="[0,0,0]" italic="false" executable="false" selection-placeholder="false" size="12" readonly="false" background="[255,255,255]" style="LaTeX" strikethrough="false" placeholder="false" family="Times New Roman" font_style_name="LaTeX">?''</Font>.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L426" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">There are many simplification strategies/commands in Maple, and I cannot review them all here. Have a look at <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">?simplify</Font> and its subcategories for more information. Here are a few tips.</Text-field><Text-field style="Bullet Item" layout="Bullet Item">Often, applying <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">expand</Font> and <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">factor</Font> sequentially to an expression gives more satisfactory results than just <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">simplify</Font><Font mathvariant="normal" mathbackground="[255,255,255]" mathsize="12" fontfamily="Times New Roman" style="Text" mathcolor="[0,0,0]">.</Font></Text-field><Text-field style="Bullet Item" layout="Bullet Item">By default, Maple assumes everything is complex-valued unless told otherwise. This can cause it to refuse to perform what look like trivial simplifications. One way around this is to use the <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">assume</Font> command.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L429" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">x := 'x':
expr := sqrt(x^2)/sqrt(-x^2);
simplify(expr);
assume(x, real);
simplify(expr);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSVleHByR0YoKiYqJEkieEdGKCIiIyMiIiJGMSwkRi8hIiIjRjVGMTcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">KigtSSVjc2duRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiNiNJInhHRigiIiJGKkYrLCQqJEYqIiIjISIiI0YvRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbW5HNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JFE2JnVtaW51czA7JkltYWdpbmFyeUk7RicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ25vcm1hbEYn">XiMhIiI=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L359" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">The assume command will ensure that whenever Maple does a calcution involving <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn</Equation>, it will assume that <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn</Equation> is real. If you would rather Maple make the assumption for just one calculation, then you could use <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">assuming</Font>:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L418" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">simplify(cos(n*Pi));
simplify(cos(n*Pi)) assuming(n, integer);
simplify(sin(n*Pi));
simplify(sin(n*Pi)) assuming(n, integer);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LUkkY29zRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiNiMqJkkibkdGJyIiIkkjUGlHRiVGKw==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">KSEiIkkibkc2Ig==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LUkkc2luRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiNiMqJkkibkdGJyIiIkkjUGlHRiVGKw==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbW5HNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JFEiMEYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdub3JtYWxGJw==">IiIh</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
</Section>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 2" layout="Heading 2">Working with and solving equations</Text-field></Title>
<Group labelreference="L428" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">restart;</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L431" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">A Maple variable can actually be an equation, or sequence of equations. Generally, any command that can be applied to an expression without an equals sign will work on an equation by operating separately on the left- and right-hand sides:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L430" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">eq := (a^2-b^2)/(a-b) = tan(theta)/sin(theta);
eq := simplify(eq);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSNlcUdGKC8qJiwmKiRJImFHRigiIiMiIiIqJEkiYkdGKEYzISIiRjQsJkYyRjRGNkY3RjcqJi1JJHRhbkdGJTYjSSZ0aGV0YUdGKEY0LUkkc2luR0YlRjxGNzcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSNlcUdGKC8sJkkiYUdGKCIiIkkiYkdGKEYxLUkkc2VjR0YlNiNJJnRoZXRhR0YoNyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L433" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">However, certain commands only work on equations, such as the closely related <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">solve</Font> and <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">isolate</Font><Font mathvariant="normal" mathbackground="[255,255,255]" mathsize="12" fontfamily="Times New Roman" style="Text" mathcolor="[0,0,0]"> commands.</Font></Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L432" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">solve(eq, theta);
isolate(eq, theta);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LUknYXJjc2VjRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiNiMsJkkiYUdGJyIiIkkiYkdGJ0Yr</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">L0kmdGhldGFHNiItSSdhcmNzZWNHNiQlKnByb3RlY3RlZEdJKF9zeXNsaWJHRiQ2IywmSSJhR0YkIiIiSSJiR0YkRi0=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L434" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">The difference between the two is that <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">isolate</Font> returns an equation with the desired variable on the left while <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">solve</Font> gives only the solution for the desired variable. Actually, the first argument of <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">solve</Font> can be any expression that is understood to be equal to zero.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L342" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">eq := a*x^2+b*x+c;
sol := solve(eq, x);
sol := [sol];</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSNlcUdGKCwoKiZJImFHRigiIiJJInhHRigiIiNGMSomSSJiR0YoRjFGMkYxRjFJImNHRihGMTcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSRzb2xHRig2JCwkKiZJImFHRighIiIsJkkiYkdGKEYyKiQsJiomRjEiIiJJImNHRihGOCEiJSokRjQiIiNGOCNGOEY8RjhGOEY9LCQqJiwmRjRGOEY1RjhGOEYxRjIjRjJGPDckRi9GPg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSRzb2xHRig3JCwkKiZJImFHRighIiIsJkkiYkdGKEYyKiQsJiomRjEiIiJJImNHRihGOCEiJSokRjQiIiNGOCNGOEY8RjhGOEY9LCQqJiwmRjRGOEY1RjhGOEYxRjIjRjJGPDcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L339" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">Notice that here, <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">solve</Font> returned the  two possible solutions for <Equation executable="false" style="Normal" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation> separated by a comma. The third line takes this output and puts it into a list. We can check that we really have solutions by using the <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">subs</Font> command to substitute our solutions back into the original expression.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L346" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">subs(x = sol[1], eq);
simplify(%);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LCgqJkkiYUc2IiEiIiwmSSJiR0YlRiYqJCwmKiZGJCIiIkkiY0dGJUYsISIlKiRGKCIiI0YsI0YsRjBGLEYwI0YsIiIlKihGKEYsRiRGJkYnRixGMUYtRiw=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbW5HNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JFEiMEYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdub3JtYWxGJw==">IiIh</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L335" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Some care must be taken with the <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">isolate</Font> command for equations with multiple solutions. We see that when we use <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">solve</Font> on a quadratic equation, we sucessfully find both roots, but when we use <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">isolate</Font>, we only get one root:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L336" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">eq := x^2+7*x+12 = 0;
solve(eq);
isolate(eq, x);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSNlcUdGKC8sKCokSSJ4R0YoIiIjIiIiRjEiIigiIzdGMyIiITcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">NiQhIiQhIiU=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">L0kieEc2IiEiJQ==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L344" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">Here is another example where we solve three equations (given as a set) for the three variables (whose solutions are returned as a set). The <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">subs</Font> command is used to pick out the particular solution for <Equation executable="false" style="Normal" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation>, <Equation executable="false" style="Normal" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEieUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEieUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation>, and <Equation executable="false" style="Normal" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiekYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiekYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation>, which we call <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">x_sol</Font>, etc.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L350" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">eqs := {2*a = x+y+z, 4*b = 2*x+z, -4*c = z+y};
sol := solve(eqs, {x, y, z});
x_sol := subs(sol, x);
y_sol := subs(sol, y);
z_sol := subs(sol, z);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSRlcXNHRig8JS8sJEkiYUdGKCIiIywoSSJ4R0YoIiIiSSJ5R0YoRjVJInpHRihGNS8sJEkiYkdGKCIiJSwmRjRGMkY3RjUvLCRJImNHRighIiUsJkY3RjVGNkY1NyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSRzb2xHRig8JS9JInhHRigsJkkiYUdGKCIiI0kiY0dGKCIiJS9JInlHRigsKEY0RjVJImJHRighIiVGMkY1L0kiekdGKCwoRjlGNUYyRjpGNCEiKTcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSZ4X3NvbEdGKCwmSSJhR0YoIiIjSSJjR0YoIiIlNyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSZ5X3NvbEdGKCwoSSJjR0YoIiIlSSJiR0YoISIlSSJhR0YoRjA3I0Yu</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSZ6X3NvbEdGKCwoSSJiR0YoIiIlSSJhR0YoISIlSSJjR0YoISIpNyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L348" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">If <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">solve</Font> fails to find an analytic solution to your problem, <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">fsolve</Font> can sometimes find a numeric one.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L353" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">eq := sin(x)-x+1/sqrt(2);
solve(eq);
sol := fsolve(eq);
simplify(subs(x = sol, eq));</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSNlcUdGKCwoLUkkc2luR0YlNiNJInhHRigiIiJGMiEiIiokIiIjI0YzRjZGNzcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LUknUm9vdE9mRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiNiMsKEkjX1pHRiQhIiMtSSRzaW5HRiQ2I0YqIiIjKiRGLyMiIiJGL0Yy</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSRzb2xHRigkIishRzYqKXAiISIqNyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">JCEiKCEjNQ==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L352" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">Here, <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">fsolve</Font> gives <Equation executable="false" style="Normal" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>, which satisfies <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">eq = 0</Font> to numeric accuracy. Finally, here are some examples of the useful <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">lhs</Font>, <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">rhs</Font><Font mathvariant="normal" mathbackground="[255,255,255]" mathsize="12" fontfamily="Times New Roman" style="Text" mathcolor="[0,0,0]">,</Font> and <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">(lhs-rhs)</Font> commands:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L357" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">eq := r^2+35 = 75*n+arctanh(r^4);
lhs(eq);
rhs(eq);
(lhs-rhs)(eq);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSNlcUdGKC8sJiokSSJyR0YoIiIjIiIiIiNORjMsJkkibkdGKCIjdi1JKGFyY3RhbmhHRiU2IyokRjEiIiVGMzcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LCYqJEkickc2IiIiIyIiIiIjTkYn</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LCZJIm5HNiIiI3YtSShhcmN0YW5oRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliR0YkNiMqJEkickdGJCIiJSIiIg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LCoqJEkickc2IiIiIyIiIiIjTkYnSSJuR0YlISN2LUkoYXJjdGFuaEc2JCUqcHJvdGVjdGVkR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJTYjKiRGJCIiJSEiIg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
</Section>
</Section>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 1" layout="Heading 1">Functions and calculus</Text-field></Title>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 2" layout="Heading 2">Defining functions as mappings</Text-field></Title>
<Group labelreference="L355" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">A mapping in Maple is an object that takes a finite number of arguments, applies some operations to them, and returns a final result. Hence, it is the Maple equivalent of a mathematical function. Mappings are defined as follows.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L360" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">f := x -&gt; x^2;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSJmR0YoZio2I0kieEdGKEYoNiRJKW9wZXJhdG9yR0YoSSZhcnJvd0dGKEYoKiQ5JCIiI0YoRihGKDcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L362" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">This mapping is called <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">f</Font>. It takes a single argument <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">x</Font> and returns its square. I can call <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">f</Font> with all sorts of arguments:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L361" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">f(x);
f(4);
f(sin(x));
expand(f(5+I*y));</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUklbXN1cEc2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy1JI21uR0YkNiRRIjJGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRicvJTFzdXBlcnNjcmlwdHNoaWZ0R1EiMEYn">KiRJInhHNiIiIiM=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbW5HNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JFEjMTZGJy8lLG1hdGh2YXJpYW50R1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">IiM7</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">KiQtSSRzaW5HNiQlKnByb3RlY3RlZEdJKF9zeXNsaWJHNiI2I0kieEdGKCIiIw==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LCgiI0QiIiIqJl4jIiM1RiRJInlHNiJGJEYkKiRGKCIiIyEiIg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L364" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">Mappings can also be defined with several arguments, and in terms of other mappings:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L363" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">g := (x, y) -&gt; x/y*sin(x*y)+f(y);
g(4, p);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSJnR0YoZio2JEkieEdGKEkieUdGKEYoNiRJKW9wZXJhdG9yR0YoSSZhcnJvd0dGKEYoLCYqKDkkIiIiLUkkc2luR0YlNiMqJjklRjhGN0Y4RjhGPSEiIkY4LUkiZkdGKDYjRj1GOEYoRihGKDcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LCYqJi1JJHNpbkc2JCUqcHJvdGVjdGVkR0koX3N5c2xpYkc2IjYjLCRJInBHRikiIiUiIiJGLCEiIkYtKiRGLCIiI0Yu</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L366" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">Note that one can also define sort of &quot;pseudo-functions'' by indescriminate use of <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">:=</Font> as shown here.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L365" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">h(x) := x^3;
h(4);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+LUkiaEdGKDYjSSJ4R0YoKiRGMCIiJDcjRjE=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LUkiaEc2IjYjIiIl</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L368" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">As you can see, <Equation executable="false" style="Normal" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiaEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy1JKG1mZW5jZWRHRiQ2JC1GIzYkLUYsNiVRInhGJ0YvRjIvRjNRJ25vcm1hbEYnRj1GPQ==">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiaEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy1JKG1mZW5jZWRHRiQ2JC1GIzYkLUYsNiVRInhGJ0YvRjIvRjNRJ25vcm1hbEYnRj1GPQ==</Equation> is not really a function at all because Maple does not know how to evaluate <Equation executable="false" style="Normal" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiaEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy1JKG1mZW5jZWRHRiQ2JC1GIzYkLUkjbW5HRiQ2JFEiNEYnL0YzUSdub3JtYWxGJ0Y+Rj5GPg==">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiaEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy1JKG1mZW5jZWRHRiQ2JC1GIzYkLUkjbW5HRiQ2JFEiNEYnL0YzUSdub3JtYWxGJ0Y+Rj5GPg==</Equation>. <Font style="Text" bold="true" italic="true">Lesson:</Font><Font style="Text" bold="true"> </Font><Font style="Text">to define a function, use mapping notation.</Font></Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
</Section>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 2" layout="Heading 2">Differentiating and integrating</Text-field></Title>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 3" layout="Heading 3">Differentiating with the &quot;diff&quot; command</Text-field></Title>
<Group labelreference="L367" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">restart;</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L369" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">The derivative of <Equation executable="false" style="Normal" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiZkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy1JKG1mZW5jZWRHRiQ2JC1GIzYkLUYsNiVRInhGJ0YvRjIvRjNRJ25vcm1hbEYnRj1GPQ==">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiZkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy1JKG1mZW5jZWRHRiQ2JC1GIzYkLUYsNiVRInhGJ0YvRjIvRjNRJ25vcm1hbEYnRj1GPQ==</Equation> with respect to <Equation executable="false" style="Normal" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation> is simply given by</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L371" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">a := diff(f(x), x);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSJhR0YoLUklZGlmZkdGJjYkLUkiZkdGKDYjSSJ4R0YoRjQ3I0Yu</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L370" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">Partial and higher order derivatives are straightforward generalizations of this.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L373" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">b := diff(g(u, v), u, u, u, v, v, u, u);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSJiR0YoLUklZGlmZkdGJjYlLUkiZ0dGKDYkSSJ1R0YoSSJ2R0YoLUkiJEdGJjYkRjQiIiYtRjc2JEY1IiIjNyMtRi82JC1GLzYkLUYvNiQtRi82JC1GLzYkLUYvNiQtRi82JEYxRjRGNEY0RjRGNEY1RjU=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L372" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">Derivatives are calculated explicitly if the quantity being differentiated is known explicitly.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L375" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">f := x -&gt; exp(sin(x)+sin(tanh(x)));
simplify(a);
diff(tan(x), x, x);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSJmR0YoZio2I0kieEdGKEYoNiRJKW9wZXJhdG9yR0YoSSZhcnJvd0dGKEYoLUkkZXhwR0YlNiMsJi1JJHNpbkdGJTYjOSQiIiItRjk2Iy1JJXRhbmhHRiVGOkY8RihGKEYoNyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">KiYtSSRleHBHNiQlKnByb3RlY3RlZEdJKF9zeXNsaWJHNiI2IywmLUkkc2luR0YlNiNJInhHRigiIiItRiw2Iy1JJXRhbmhHRiVGLUYvRi8sJi1JJGNvc0dGJUYtRi8qJi1GNkYxRi8tSSVzZWNoR0YlRi0iIiNGL0Yv</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LCQqJi1JJHRhbkc2JCUqcHJvdGVjdGVkR0koX3N5c2xpYkc2IjYjSSJ4R0YpIiIiLCZGLEYsKiRGJCIiI0YsRixGLw==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L374" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">You can even differentiate equations.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L377" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">eq := x^2 = tan(x)^(1/4);
diff(eq, x);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSNlcUdGKC8qJEkieEdGKCIiIyokLUkkdGFuR0YlNiNGMCMiIiIiIiU3I0Yu</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LywkSSJ4RzYiIiIjLCQqJi1JJHRhbkc2JCUqcHJvdGVjdGVkR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJTYjRiQjISIkIiIlLCYiIiJGMyokRilGJkYzRjMjRjNGMQ==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
</Section>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 3" layout="Heading 3">Differentiating with the D operator</Text-field></Title>
<Group labelreference="L376" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">The <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">D</Font> operator differentiates an expression with respect to its argument(s) while <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">diff</Font> differentiates with respect to variables. This is best illustrated by example.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L379" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">f := x -&gt; sin(x);
a := diff(f(q(x)), x);
b := D(f)(q(x));</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSJmR0YoZio2I0kieEdGKEYoNiRJKW9wZXJhdG9yR0YoSSZhcnJvd0dGKEYoLUkkc2luR0YlNiM5JEYoRihGKDcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSJhR0YoKiYtSSVkaWZmR0YmNiQtSSJxR0YoNiNJInhHRihGNSIiIi1JJGNvc0dGJTYjRjJGNjcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSJiR0YoLUkkY29zR0YlNiMtSSJxR0YoNiNJInhHRig3I0Yu</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L378" drawlabel="true">
