</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L400" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">In this procedure, the last line of output depends on what type of argument we have. The <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">true</Font> and <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">false</Font> quantities are special in Maple because there are the arguments of <Font mathvariant="bold" mathbackground="[255,255,255]" fontweight="bold" mathsize="12" fontfamily="Courier New" style="Maple Input" mathcolor="[120,0,14]" executable="false">if</Font>/<Font mathvariant="bold" mathbackground="[255,255,255]" fontweight="bold" mathsize="12" fontfamily="Courier New" style="Maple Input" mathcolor="[120,0,14]" executable="false">then</Font> structures. Indeed, <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">true</Font><Font mathvariant="normal" mathbackground="[255,255,255]" mathsize="12" fontfamily="Times New Roman" style="Text" mathcolor="[0,0,0]">/</Font><Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">false</Font> is what the <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">type</Font> function returns.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L399" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">type(5, prime);
type(6, prime);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbWlHNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JVEldHJ1ZUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR0YrLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJw==">SSV0cnVlRyUqcHJvdGVjdGVkRw==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbWlHNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JVEmZmFsc2VGJy8lJ2l0YWxpY0dRJXRydWVGJy8lLG1hdGh2YXJpYW50R1EnaXRhbGljRic=">SSZmYWxzZUclKnByb3RlY3RlZEc=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L405" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">Because our <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">HalfInteger</Font> procedure is <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">true</Font><Font mathvariant="normal" mathbackground="[255,255,255]" mathsize="12" fontfamily="Times New Roman" style="Text" mathcolor="[0,0,0]">/</Font><Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">false</Font> valued, it could be used in further <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">if</Font><Font mathvariant="normal" mathbackground="[255,255,255]" mathsize="12" fontfamily="Times New Roman" style="Text" mathcolor="[0,0,0]">/</Font><Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">then</Font> statements.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L404" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">PositiveHalfInteger := proc(x)
    if HalfInteger(x) and x&gt;0 then:
        &quot;Congratulations! You have found a positive half integer! Call Sweden!&quot;:
    else:
        &quot;I am sorry. This is not what we are looking for. Please don't give up.&quot;:
    fi:
end proc:
PositiveHalfInteger(-5/2);
PositiveHalfInteger(5/2);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbXNHNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2I1Fhb0l+YW1+c29ycnkuflRoaXN+aXN+bm90fndoYXR+d2V+YXJlfmxvb2tpbmd+Zm9yLn5QbGVhc2V+ZG9uJ3R+Z2l2ZX51cC5GJw==">UWFvSX5hbX5zb3JyeS5+VGhpc35pc35ub3R+d2hhdH53ZX5hcmV+bG9va2luZ35mb3IuflBsZWFzZX5kb24ndH5naXZlfnVwLjYi</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbXNHNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2I1Fgb0NvbmdyYXR1bGF0aW9ucyF+WW91fmhhdmV+Zm91bmR+YX5wb3NpdGl2ZX5oYWxmfmludGVnZXIhfkNhbGx+U3dlZGVuIUYn">UWBvQ29uZ3JhdHVsYXRpb25zIX5Zb3V+aGF2ZX5mb3VuZH5hfnBvc2l0aXZlfmhhbGZ+aW50ZWdlciF+Q2FsbH5Td2VkZW4hNiI=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
